js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:17:3: error: the length of an array cannot be assigned
  = note: to shorten it, write `xs.truncate(n)`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:18:9: error: variable `sorted` cannot have type `void`
  = note: `sort` changes the array in place and returns nothing (unlike JS): for a sorted copy, call `toSorted` instead of `sort`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:19:9: error: variable `copy` cannot have type `void`
  = note: `reverse` changes the array in place and returns nothing (unlike JS): for a reversed copy, call `toReversed` instead of `reverse`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:20:9: error: variable `filled` cannot have type `void`
  = note: `fill` changes the array in place and returns nothing (unlike JS): call it, then use `xs`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:21:9: error: variable `zeros` cannot have type `void`
  = note: `fill` changes the array in place and returns nothing (unlike JS): store the array in a variable first (`const a = …; a.fill(v);`), then use `a`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:23:9: error: variable `shuffled` cannot have type `void`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:24:36: error: no method named `then` found for type `Promise<i64>`
  = note: promises take no callbacks: `await` the promise, inside `try`/`catch`/`finally` to handle its error
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:25:15: error: `process.stdout` is not a value: use its members
  = note: call `process.stdout.write(s)`; for bytes, `import { stdout } from "velt:process"`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:26:29: error: `process.env` is not a value: use its members
  = note: read a variable with `process.env.NAME` or `process.env[name]` (`string | null`); set one with `setEnv(name, value)` of `velt:process`; list them all with `envAll()` of `velt:process` (a `Record<string, string>`)
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:27:3: error: cannot assign to `process.env`
  = note: use `setEnv(name, value)` from `velt:process` (not synchronized with reads on other threads: set variables at startup)
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:28:10: error: cannot `delete` from `process.env`
  = note: use `removeEnv(name)` from `velt:process`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:29:16: error: `process.exit` can only be called
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:30:17: error: `process.memoryUsage` can only be called
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:31:15: error: `process.pid` is not supported
  = note: the builtin `process` has `process.env.NAME`, `process.stdout.write(s)`, `process.argv`, `process.exit(code)` and `process.memoryUsage()`; `cwd()` is in `velt:process`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:32:18: error: `process.stdout` has no method `end`
  = note: use `write(s)`, or `velt:process` for byte writes
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:33:16: error: `process.argv` can't be changed in place: each read is a new array
  = note: TypeScript allows this (Node keeps one array, so changes persist), but in Velt the change would be lost; copy it first: `const argv = process.argv`, then change `argv`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:34:3: error: `process.argv` can't be changed in place: each read is a new array
  = note: TypeScript allows this (Node keeps one array, so changes persist), but in Velt the change would be lost; copy it first: `const argv = process.argv`, then change `argv`
js_array_and_promise_idioms.vlt:35:3: error: `process.argv` can't be changed in place: each read is a new array
  = note: TypeScript allows this (Node keeps one array, so changes persist), but in Velt the change would be lost; copy it first: `const argv = process.argv`, then change `argv`
